🌍 About the Company
The client is a Cyprus-based FinTech and software development company building digital products for businesses and individual users . Its product portfolio covers payment integrations, crypto-to-fiat exchange, trading platforms, CRM systems, and mobile applications.
The company develops scalable solutions for use across different markets and jurisdictions. Its next priority is to turn a secure messaging application, originally created for internal communication, into a commercial product for external business clients.
💼 About the Role
As IT Project Manager , you will lead the messenger application through its next stage: from an established internal tool to a commercially viable B2B platform.
You will coordinate product, engineering, design, testing, and commercial stakeholders while creating a clear roadmap for development, launch, and customer adoption. This role offers substantial ownership over both delivery and the future direction of the product.
🔍 Responsibilities

• Own the end-to-end project roadmap, from product assessment and commercial requirements to launch and ongoing development;

• Translate business goals and customer needs into clear specifications, priorities, milestones, and delivery plans;

• Coordinate mobile and backend developers, QA specialists, designers, and other contributors across the software development lifecycle;

• Establish delivery processes, sprint cadences, documentation standards, and reliable progress reporting;

• Manage project scope, dependencies, budgets, timelines, and risks while keeping stakeholders aligned;

• Work with commercial teams to define the product proposition, target customer segments, implementation model, and launch priorities;

• Guide the development of business-ready functionality, including administration, user management, security, integrations, and support processes;

• Coordinate testing, release readiness, feedback collection, and continuous product improvements;

• Monitor delivery and adoption metrics, identify bottlenecks, and recommend practical improvements.

🎓 Requirements
Must Have

• 3+ years of experience managing software, mobile application, SaaS, or other technology projects;

• Demonstrated ownership of projects across discovery, planning, development, testing, release, and post-launch improvement;

• Strong understanding of Agile delivery methods and modern software development processes;

• Experience coordinating cross-functional teams and converting business requirements into actionable technical work;

• Ability to manage competing priorities, delivery risks, dependencies, and stakeholder expectations;

• Working knowledge of project management and documentation tools such as Jira and Confluence or comparable platforms;

• Professional fluency in English, with clear written and verbal communication skills;

• A structured, hands-on approach and the confidence to make decisions in an evolving product environment.

Nice to Have

• Experience launching or commercialising an internal product for external B2B customers;

• Background in messaging, collaboration tools, mobile applications, FinTech, payments, or SaaS;

• Familiarity with data privacy, application security, encrypted communication, or enterprise access controls;

• Experience supporting customer onboarding, third-party integrations, or go-to-market planning.

🤝 Key Competencies

• Strong ownership and accountability for delivery outcomes;

• Clear communication across technical, commercial, and senior stakeholder groups;

• Sound judgement when balancing speed, scope, quality, and customer value;

• Ability to bring structure to ambiguous requirements and changing priorities;

• Commercial awareness combined with a practical understanding of technology.

